# basePath SupplyIntroCh2

:: StartBuilding
@trigger    OnSupplySetupCompleted
@when   !MinigameHasValidSolution()
$call   PointElement(supply:planet_sio2converter)
{@PAL}  You need a semiconductor, so you'll need to take the quartz to a refining station.


:: NodeClicked
@trigger    OnNodeClicked
@when   !MinigameHasValidSolution()
$call   ReleaseAllHighlights()
$call   CloseWiki()
$if     !temp:firstNodeClicked
    $set    temp:firstNodeClicked = true
    {@PAL}  Use the <color=yellow>WASD</color> or <color=yellow>Arrow</color> keys to move around and find other planets.
$elseif !temp:secondNodeClicked
    $set    temp:secondNodeClicked = true
    $call   PointElement(supply:ship0-time)
    {@PAL}  The planets with the highest time determines the total production time of your route.
$endif

:: RouteCompleted
@trigger    OnRouteCompleted
@when   !MinigameHasValidSolution()
$call   ReleaseAllHighlights()
$call   CloseWiki()
$if !IsMaterialCollected("Silicon")
    {@PAL}  You need a semiconductor, so you'll need to take the quartz to a refining station.
$elseif !IsMaterialCollected("Copper")
    {@PAL}	Use the <color=yellow>WASD</color> or <color=yellow>Arrow</color> keys to move around and find other planets.
$else
    $call   PointElement(supply:ship0-time)
    {@PAL}  The route time is production time + travel time.\n\nTravel time is based on the distance and the speed of the ship.
$endif

:: OnRoutesConfirmed
@trigger    OnRoutesConfirmed
$call   ReleaseAllHighlights()
$call   CloseWiki()
{@PAL} Once you confirm your route, all materials are ordered at the same time.\n\nEach route time is based on the longest production time on that route plus the travel time.